path: /
title: The School Manager: school management software for Pakistan
description: School management software for Pakistani private schools. One parent pays once for all their children, and you see what was owed. From Rs 950 a month.
schema: org software
priority: 1.0
changefreq: weekly
---
<header class="hero" id="top">
  <div class="wrap hero__grid">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Built for Pakistani schools</span>
      <h1>One parent. One payment. <em>One receipt.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A father with three children hands over one bundle of cash. Most software
        makes your clerk do that three times. This does it once, and tells you at
        the end of the month exactly how much should have come in and how much
        actually did.
      </p>
      <div class="hero__cta">
        <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/pricing" data-app="signup">Start 14 day free trial</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/fee-management">See how fees work</a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero__note">No card required. Set up in an afternoon. Your data stays yours.</p>
      <p id="signup-closed" hidden class="hero__note">
        We are at capacity this month. Get in touch and we will put you next in line.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="app">
      <div class="app__bar" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="app__dot"></span><span class="app__dot"></span><span class="app__dot"></span>
        <span class="app__url">Fees, collect</span>
      </div>
      <div class="app__body">
        <div class="app__side" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="app__brand">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <rect width="24" height="24" rx="6" fill="#4F46E5"/>
              <g fill="#fff"><circle cx="12" cy="7.5" r="1.4"/><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M5.5 12.5h13v6h-13zm2.5 1.5h8v1h-8zm0 2h8v1h-8z"/></g>
            </svg>
            Al-Noor School
          </div>
          <div class="app__nav">
            <span>Dashboard</span>
            <span>Admissions</span>
            <span>Students</span>
            <span>Attendance</span>
            <span class="on">Fees</span>
            <span>Exams</span>
            <span>Accounts</span>
            <span>Reports</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="app__main">
          <div class="app__tiles">
            <div class="tile tile--money"><span>Collected</span><b class="tnum">Rs 84,500</b></div>
            <div class="tile tile--due"><span>Outstanding</span><b class="tnum">Rs 312,000</b></div>
            <div class="tile"><span>Students</span><b class="tnum">486</b></div>
          </div>
          <div class="app__rows">
            <div class="arow"><b>Muhammad Aslam</b><span class="muted">3 children</span></div>
            <div class="arow"><span>Ahmed, Class 5</span><span class="pill pill--paid">Paid</span></div>
            <div class="arow"><span>Fatima, Class 3</span><span class="pill pill--paid">Paid</span></div>
            <div class="arow"><span>Bilal, Play Group</span><span class="pill pill--due">Rs 1,200 due</span></div>
            <div class="arow"><b>One receipt</b><b class="tnum">Rs 5,800</b></div>
          </div>
          <div class="chart" aria-hidden="true">
            <i style="height:44%"></i><i style="height:62%"></i><i style="height:53%"></i>
            <i style="height:78%"></i><i style="height:66%"></i><i style="height:88%"></i>
            <i style="height:72%"></i><i style="height:96%"></i>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- ================================================================= trust
     A breath between the hero and the first section. The previous version cut
     straight from a cream hero into a full-bleed navy slab, which is the
     jarring transition.
     ================================================================= -->
<div class="trust">
  <div class="wrap trust__in">
    <div class="trust__cell">
      <span class="trust__k">From</span>
      <span class="trust__v"><b id="lead-price">Rs 950</b> <small>a month</small></span>
    </div>
    <div class="trust__cell">
      <span class="trust__k">Trial</span>
      <span class="trust__v">14 days <small>no card</small></span>
    </div>
    <div class="trust__cell">
      <span class="trust__k">Modules</span>
      <span class="trust__v">All included <small>every plan</small></span>
    </div>
    <div class="trust__cell">
      <span class="trust__k">Runs on</span>
      <span class="trust__v">Any browser <small>no install</small></span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- =========================================================== what it does ===
     Nine capabilities, each linking to the page that covers it properly. This
     replaces the old feature grid whose cards linked nowhere: a visitor who
     wanted to know how fees actually work had no next page to go to, and
     neither did a search engine. -->
<section class="section" id="what">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">What it does</span>
    <h2>The whole school, not just the fee counter</h2>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:12px">
      One price. Every module. No add-ons to buy later.
    </p>

    <div class="grid grid--3" style="margin-top:38px">
      <a class="card card--link" href="/fee-management">
        <h3>Fees and challans</h3>
        <p>
          One parent pays once for all their children. Monthly challans, arrears
          carried forward, partial payments, fines, approved discounts, and a
          receipt number that cannot skip.
        </p>
        <span class="card__more">How fee collection works</span>
      </a>
      <a class="card card--link" href="/attendance">
        <h3>Attendance</h3>
        <p>
          A daily register per class, marked from a phone in the classroom, that
          keeps working when the internet does not. Finalise, lock, and print the
          monthly sheet.
        </p>
        <span class="card__more">How attendance works</span>
      </a>
      <a class="card card--link" href="/exams-and-results">
        <h3>Exams and result cards</h3>
        <p>
          Marks per paper, practicals and weightage, grades computed on your own
          scale, then printed result cards, tabulation sheets and class positions.
        </p>
        <span class="card__more">How exams work</span>
      </a>
      <a class="card card--link" href="/accounts">
        <h3>Accounts and payroll</h3>
        <p>
          An expense ledger with categories, other income, cash drawer sessions,
          a day book, staff salaries, and the monthly profit that follows from
          all of it.
        </p>
        <span class="card__more">How the accounts work</span>
      </a>
      <a class="card card--link" href="/parent-portal">
        <h3>Parent portal</h3>
        <p>
          Parents sign in on their own phone and see their own children only:
          balance, every receipt, attendance day by day, and results once you
          publish them.
        </p>
        <span class="card__more">How the portal works</span>
      </a>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>And the rest of it</h3>
        <p>
          Admissions with automatic GR numbers and sibling linking. Staff records
          and teacher logins. Leaving, character and bonafide certificates on
          tracked serial registers. Student and staff ID cards. Year end rollover
          for the whole school in one pass.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================================================================ records ===-->
<section class="section section--tint" id="records">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Your records</span>
      <h2>Your records leave with you</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:12px">
        Export everything you have entered, at any time, in a plain readable
        format, including on the day you decide to leave. There is no lock in
        and no fee for your own data.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-top:16px">
        And nothing is ever quietly removed. A wrong entry is corrected by a
        reversal, so both lines stay in the record with a reason and a name. If
        somebody asks in two years why a receipt was cancelled, the answer is
        still there.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-top:20px">
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/faq">Read the questions principals ask</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <div class="panel__head">
        <span class="panel__title">Audit trail</span>
        <span class="panel__sub">Muhammad Aslam</span>
      </div>
      <div class="app__rows" style="border:0;border-radius:0">
        <div class="arow"><span>Receipt 1041<br><small>Asif Mehmood, class 5</small></span><b>Rs 1,700</b></div>
        <div class="arow"><span>Reversal of 1041<br><small>Wrong pupil, entered 09:12</small></span><b>(Rs 1,700)</b></div>
        <div class="arow"><span>Posted to the wrong child</span><span class="pill pill--paid">Net Rs 0</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="panel__foot">
        Neither line is struck out, because neither line happened by accident. This
        is what answers the question two years later.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ==================================================================== cta ===-->
<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cta on-dark">
      <h2>Try it with one class first</h2>
      <p>
        Fourteen days, no card, no commitment. Put one class in, run a month's
        challans, and see whether the numbers agree with your register.
      </p>
      <div class="cta__row">
        <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/pricing" data-app="signup">Start your free trial</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/contact">Talk to a person first</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
